{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794297299,"nonce":"Ad5dPc/9xR0OjGMaHNwWqqhEzlY=","title":"A primitive missing from an optional library (\"?lib\") aborts the run instead of raising when called","message":"HashLink binds a native whose library is optional (`@:hlNative(\"?sdl\", ...)`, written `?sdl` in the bytecode) to `hl_prim_not_loaded` when the HDLL does not export it (module.c, hl_module_init_natives: `if (is_opt) { functions_ptrs[n-\u003efindex] = hl_prim_not_loaded; continue; }`). The program starts, and the call raises a catchable \"Primitive or library is missing\". Ash does not honour the `?`: every tier fails hard.\n\nReproducer (crates/ash/test/hdll_release/OptionalPrim.hx plus any sdl.hdll that lacks the names), expected HashLink output `start / after-skip / caught: Primitive or library is missing / end`. Observed on macOS with the arm64 sdl.hdll from examples/heaps_base2d:\n- interp, hybrid: `start`, `after-skip`, then `Error: dlsym(...): symbol not found` and the run ends. The error is not catchable.\n- jit: `Uncaught exception: JIT tier 0 failed to compile findex 29`; the program never starts, although the first primitive is never called.\n\nWhere it comes from: NativeLibraryManager::resolve_function_uncached propagates the lookup error with `?`; the interpreter (ash_interp interpreter/natives.rs) and the JIT tiers treat it as fatal. Ash already has the pieces: hlp_prim_not_loaded and hlp_is_prim_loaded in std/src/fun.rs, and the LLVM tier's ASH_JIT_NATIVE_TRAPS call-time trap.\n\nWhy it matters (GitHub issue #1, Windows): a project built from the released haxelibs (heaps 2.1.0, hlsdl 1.16.0, haxeui 1.7.0) names `?sdl@win_get_display_scale`. hlsdl 1.16.0 declares it, and DCE keeps every field of a library class, so the bytecode names it although nothing calls it. HashLink's 1.15 sdl.hdll (SDL2) lacks it; 1.16 has it (HashLink PR 955, merged 2026-07-10, in 1.16 not 1.15; Heaps PR 1356 merged 2026-07-23). Stock HashLink therefore runs that program on 1.15 HDLLs; ash ends with `Error: GetProcAddress failed ... (os error 127)`, which is the reporter's output. Not Windows-specific.\n\nFix: bind a missing primitive of a `?`-prefixed library to hlp_prim_not_loaded in the symbol table and in every resolver (interpreter, Cranelift, LLVM, AOT), so it raises when called and hl.Api.isPrimLoaded reports it false. A missing primitive of a non-optional library keeps failing at load, as HashLink does (`Failed to load function lib@name`), and that message should name both.\n\nThe dry run in .github/workflows/hdll_release_probe.yml (branch ci/hdll-release-probe) runs this reproducer and the reporter's HaxeUI project against HashLink's official 1.15 and 1.16 Windows HDLLs. The unrelated commit b5ad62c1 (error text for a missing primitive) gives advice that is wrong for optional primitives and should be revisited with the fix.","files":null}]}